# API contracts

Canonical spec: `docs/api.md`. Prefix `/api/v1`. Errors `{ "detail": "..." }`.

- Pydantic v2 for every request/response. No ad-hoc dict contracts.
- Auth on all `/api/v1/*` except login/register/google. Identity from cookies (`dw_*`) only — ignore `Authorization: Bearer`. Never from body `user_id` / `access_roles`.
- Resource ids are UUID strings, including chat citations `doc_id`.
- Upload returns `201` + `pending` and enqueues Celery. Do not parse PDF in the handler.
- `GET /documents` and `/raw` apply the same ACL as search. Missing-or-forbidden → `404`, not a leaky `403` with the title.
- Delete is cascade: Postgres (document + chunks) + MinIO.

## SSE `POST /api/v1/chat/stream`

ChainWise envelopes (not named `event:` from the draft TZ):

```
data: {"type":"citations","citations":[{"doc_id":"<uuid>","doc_title":"Travel.pdf","page":4,"snippet":"..."}]}

data: {"type":"token","content":"..."}

data: {"type":"meta","tokens_used":640}

data: [DONE]
```

Citations first, then tokens. On failure: `{"type":"error","content":"..."}` — no stack, no foreign document titles.

Inspect is admin/dev only (`ENABLE_SEARCH_INSPECT`). Same ACL filter as chat.
